  "notes": "USAGE:\nA key term in discussions of government benefits, social security, and insurance in Japan. Became widely known during the COVID-19 pandemic when the government distributed {特別定額給付金|とくべつていがくきゅうふきん} (special fixed-amount benefits) to all residents.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {支給|しきゅう}: provision, supply (from an employer or organization)\n- {手当|てあて}: allowance, benefit (often for specific purposes like commuting)\n- {補助金|ほじょきん}: subsidy, grant (for projects or organizations)\n\nWATCH OUT:\nNot to be confused with {休符|きゅうふ} (musical rest).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {給付金|きゅうふきん}: benefit payment, subsidy\n- {失業|しつぎょう}{給付|きゅうふ}: unemployment benefits\n- {給付|きゅうふ}を{受|う}ける: to receive benefits\n- {給付|きゅうふ}{対象|たいしょう}: eligible for benefits\n- {現金|げんきん}{給付|きゅうふ}: cash benefit",
